course: dictionary
lesson: 15967
title: Can you check it?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Verify means to check that something is true. The un- at the start means not, so unverifiable means impossible to check or prove true or false. «Ella said her gran once met a dragon, but nobody saw it and there is no photo.» Nobody can check this claim, so it is unverifiable.
explain: Good readers ask: Is there a source? Is there evidence? Can I test it? If the answer to all three is no, the claim may be unverifiable. Being unable to check something does not always make it false, but it means you should not believe it just because someone said it.
explain: The word is often used with «claims» and «rumours», especially on the internet. «The post had an unverifiable rumour about a secret school closure» means that nobody could prove or disprove the rumour. In science, a good idea must be testable, so an unverifiable idea cannot be tested and cannot be a scientific fact.
fact: Un- means not, and verify means to check that something is true.
fact: «Unverifiable» means impossible to check or prove true or false.
fact: An unverifiable claim has no source, no evidence and no way to check it.
fact: In science, a good idea must be testable; an unverifiable idea cannot be tested.
fact: Useful phrases: «unverifiable claims» and «unverifiable rumours».
exercise: «Sam said his cat can talk, but there is no video, no witness and no way to check it.» What does unverifiable mean? | Funny | Easy to believe and to share | Very large | *Impossible to check or prove true or false
exercise: «The rumour had no source and no evidence at all.» What does this tell you about the rumour? | *It is unverifiable, because nobody can check it | It has been proved false by a scientist | It is a famous news story | It is definitely true
exercise: An idea that nobody can test is called ... | simple | verified | proven | *unverifiable
test: Which sentence shows an unverifiable claim? | Water boils at 100 degrees at sea level | Two plus two is four | The sun rose at six this morning | *The man said he saw a flying cow, but nobody can check it
test: What does the un- in unverifiable mean? | *Not | Very much | Again | Before
exam: Ravi reads «unverifiable rumours» online. What should he do first? | Share them quickly with his friends | Skip the word and read on | *Look for a source and evidence before believing or sharing | Believe them because they are online
